o's Moderna Museet (1998) on Skeppsholmen, Stockholm, from published descriptions (the museum, Moneo's office, Arquitectura Viva) and the ground file's footprint (a long low building turned about 48 degrees, down the island's spine): square and rectangular galleries of varying sizes 'bundled' into fragments, each under a pyramidal roof crowned by a rectangular lantern, in red-ochre render with zinc roofs; the long, top-lit entrance hall and street on the south-west side; the older armoury (Tyghuset) to the north-west; the island's trees. Guessed: the render colour, the rooms' exact sizes and arrangement, heights, the lantern proportions. No photographs were available."}